  {
   "id": "a_M33kYzBAAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-05-04T11:25:23Z",
   "subject": "Re: Can blavan handle categorical data?",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>When you say that Blavaan does not currently support categorical variables, does this include exogenous covariates as well?</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>No, there are no distributional assumptions about exogenous variables, so it is arbitrary whether they are continuous or discrete.  For proper interpretation, it is up to you to include dummy codes that make sense.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463545226000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2SmksKNqLthX4RmWgOLGsy\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
